  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Construct the matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T$ that acts on a vector in ${R}^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- It stretches the result by a scale factor of $3$ parallel to the $x$-axis, then\n\n- shears the result with a shear factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis, and finally\n\n- reflects the result about the $x$-axis.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |",
  "worked_solution": "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the stretching, $Q$ be the matrix that represents the shearing, and $R$ be the matrix that represents the reflection. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\,\n$$\n\nHence, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $RQP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =RQP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
